{
  "$comment": "Spelling chg's lexical forms (docs/rules/chg.md): chg-Arab/standard's `spell` statement (profiles/chg-Arab.standard.yaml), run by @nabu/core over forms in chg's notation (lexicons/chg/language.yaml), realised ones with their boundaries (+), which the statement keeps for its rules (`boundaries: true`: where a suffix joins, after a half-space or not). spell/fixture/boundaries/* run a statement and notation of their own; spell/chg/* one vector or more per rule of chg-Arab/standard's statement, each a word of the course.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "id": "spell/fixture/boundaries/kept",
      "op": "spell",
      "args": {
        "profile": {
          "id": "und-Latn/fixture",
          "lang": "und-Latn",
          "segmentation": {
            "content": "hand-pinned",
            "runtime": "grapheme"
          },
          "normalize": [],
          "spell": {
            "from": "lexical",
            "boundaries": true,
            "rules": [
              {
                "find": "\\+",
                "after": "{C}",
                "to": "",
                "alternatives": [
                  {
                    "id": "hyphen",
                    "to": "-"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "notation": {
          "sets": {
            "C": "[bcdfgklmnpqrstwz]",
            "V": "[aeiou]"
          }
        },
        "form": "kat+lar"
      },
      "expected": {
        "spelling": "katlar",
        "alternatives": [
          {
            "spelling": "kat-lar",
            "by": [
              "hyphen"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "`boundaries: true`: a rule names the boundary (+) of a realised form (here: after a consonant, written joined or with a hyphen, freely); what is left of the boundaries is dropped after the rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "spell/fixture/boundaries/not-there",
      "op": "spell",
      "args": {
        "profile": {
          "id": "und-Latn/fixture",
          "lang": "und-Latn",
          "segmentation": {
            "content": "hand-pinned",
            "runtime": "grapheme"
          },
          "normalize": [],
          "spell": {
            "from": "lexical",
            "boundaries": true,
            "rules": [
              {
                "find": "\\+",
                "after": "{C}",
                "to": "",
                "alternatives": [
                  {
                    "id": "hyphen",
                    "to": "-"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "notation": {
          "sets": {
            "C": "[bcdfgklmnpqrstwz]",
            "V": "[aeiou]"
          }
        },
        "form": "kala+lar"
      },
      "expected": {
        "spelling": "kalalar",
        "alternatives": []
      },
      "note": "A boundary no rule names (after a vowel) is dropped after the rules, as it would have been before them."
    },
    {
      "id": "spell/fixture/boundaries/each-place",
      "op": "spell",
      "args": {
        "profile": {
          "id": "und-Latn/fixture",
          "lang": "und-Latn",
          "segmentation": {
            "content": "hand-pinned",
            "runtime": "grapheme"
          },
          "normalize": [],
          "spell": {
            "from": "lexical",
            "boundaries": true,
            "rules": [
              {
                "find": "\\+",
                "after": "{C}",
                "to": "",
                "alternatives": [
                  {
                    "id": "hyphen",
                    "to": "-"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "notation": {
          "sets": {
            "C": "[bcdfgklmnpqrstwz]",
            "V": "[aeiou]"
          }
        },
        "form": "kat+lar+dan"
      },
      "expected": {
        "spelling": "katlardan",
        "alternatives": [
          {
            "spelling": "katlar-dan",
            "by": [
              "hyphen"
            ]
          },
          {
            "spelling": "kat-lardan",
            "by": [
              "hyphen"
            ]
          },
          {
            "spelling": "kat-lar-dan",
            "by": [
              "hyphen"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": "An alternative at a boundary is a choice at each place it holds."
    },
    {
      "id": "spell/fixture/boundaries/dropped-first",
      "op": "spell",
      "args": {
        "profile": {
          "id": "und-Latn/fixture",
          "lang": "und-Latn",
          "segmentation": {
            "content": "hand-pinned",
            "runtime": "grapheme"
          },
          "normalize": [],
          "spell": {
            "from": "lexical",
            "rules": [
              {
                "find": "\\+",
                "after": "{C}",
                "to": "",
                "alternatives": [
                  {
                    "id": "hyphen",
                    "to": "-"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "notation": {
          "sets": {
            "C": "[bcdfgklmnpqrstwz]",
            "V": "[aeiou]"
          }
        },
        "form": "kat+lar"
      },
      "expected": {
        "spelling": "katlar",
        "alternatives": []
      },
      "note": "Without `boundaries` they are dropped first, as before: the rule never sees one."
    }
  ]
}
